<article class="env-remark" id="06H8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06H8">Remark <span data-tag="06H8">90.7.6</span>.</a> Let $F: \mathcal{C}_\Lambda \to \textit{Sets}$ be a functor. Identifying functors with cofibered sets, the completion of $F$ is the functor $\widehat{F} : \widehat{\mathcal{C}}_\Lambda \to \textit{Sets}$ given by $\widehat{F}(S) = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits F(S/\mathfrak {m}_ S^{n})$. This agrees with the definition in Schlessinger's paper <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Sch">Sch</a>]</span>. </p>
</article>